review:
I love the visuals and animations, and the core idea of being a merchant and delving into dungeons is great but the execution is lacking, it feels like it's in Early Access.
The game is repetitive not because of its loop but because of its lack of polish and depth.


There is no keyboard support, if you don't have a controller don't buy this game;
Combat is super clunky and unbalanced, it lacks a lot of fluidity, you can't cancel animations and general controls are a pain in the ass, good luck rolling diagonally or over pools of lava and poison; 
Dungeons are poorly designed, 80% of rooms are filled with holes and pools of goop that will damage you (this is frustrating and not fun, you often lose more runs due to room layouts than to the enemies), and there is also a lot of backtracking because there are no teleports or shortcuts that bring you to previous rooms; there are secret rooms, which are way too common and with some being way too useful forcing the player to be constantly looking out for them, there is also a secret room that brings you to a special floor that if you complete it you obtain a unique weapon that only lasts the current run, you would think this weapon is crazy good but this weapon sucks more ass than your normal weapons.
The player progression is dull, both weapons and armour have you upgrading their tiers in a straight line, with armour the only stats you have are Health, Defense and MovSpeed and with weapons you just choose if you want flat damage or flat elemental damage, the weapons movesets also never change throughout the game.
After your first dungeon you already know how the rest of the game is going to play out;
The story is poorly delivered, there are lore notes in the dungeons but these are RANDOM meaning it's hard to tell which ones you've already read, the same thing with NPCs and its also unfortunate that these don't give you any unique quests or useful information (as far as I know);
Managing your store is fine, IF the game didn't already have such glaring problems, besides basic is also needs severe quality of life improvements, little is properly explained on how it works, forcing you to search most of the information from the wiki and reddit; pricing your materials is a bit of an hassle, the system is weird and it doesn't make sense how there's no proper price estimation considering there is clearly an already established local economy, the law of supply and demand doesn't work like it should and you can't hire employees to help you out, i mean, it's actually possible to hire a "shop assistant" if you could actually call it that, this NPC will "steal" a staggering 30% of your sales for some damn reason.
You can improve your shop by expanding it and buying decorations but this also has cons, upgrading your shop expands your interior, allowing you to sell more items and put more decoration which give useful stats to help you sell more efficiently, but, the only inside decoration you have control over are objects you place in specific places and there are also no exterior visual changes at all (yes its just visual and would not change gameplay but it would be a welcome sight to see your shop become larger and cooler due to your efforts).
